<Project Version="4" Seed="2101">
	<Description>Lighthouse lens: a point source at the focus of a Fresnel lens collimates the light into a parallel beam. Frequency 150 (wavelength 10.7 px, so the outer zones stay a few wavelengths wide); a lens of index 1.5, diameter 400, radii 600 and -600 (focal length 600, f/1.5), its plate 24 px thick and each surface cut into 3 zones of equal depth, 11.4 px each, the zones narrowing outward from 232 px to 36 px; the lamp 600 px before the lens, an absorbing mount around it. The line probe Beam reads the collimated beam 450 px after the lens.</Description>
	<Scene Width="1280" Height="600" />
	<Simulation Steps="2000" />
